---
// MqTopology: the FairMQ devices of a FairRoot MQ example, animated. Boxes are the devices of the start
// script (device ID and class or program), lines are the channels (name and socket type at each end,
// a filled dot where the socket binds, an open dot where it connects), and squares are the messages.
// The prop `example` selects the topology: 'pixel' (default), 'split' or 'serialization'.
// Paths are relative to the FairRoot repository.
//
// pixel: examples/MQ/pixelDetector/run/scripts/startFairMQPixel.sh.in
// - Server: parmq-server --id pixDet-parmq-server, channel param rep bind tcp://*:5405 (117-120). The program makes a
//   ParameterMQServer (fairroot/parmq/runParameterMQServer.cxx:39), --channel-name param makes OnData(param,
//   ProcessRequest) (fairroot/parmq/ParameterMQServer.cxx:45-56). ProcessRequest() reads "<name>,<run ID>", gets the
//   container from the runtime database and replies with it, serialized with RootSerializer (117-164).
// - Sampler: pixel-sampler --id pixDet-sampler1, data-out push bind tcp://*:5406 (123-126). The program makes a
//   FairMQPixelSampler (run/runPixelSampler.cxx:41). ConditionalRun() reads one event and sends one multipart message
//   with one part for each branch, here PixelDigis and EventHeader. (FairMQPixelSampler.cxx:100-123; script 83, 130).
// - Processors: NOFPROCESSORS=3 (15) is the default of -p, --nof-processors (41-42); IDs pixDet-processor1 … N
//   (141-144). Channels: param req connect :5405, data-in pull connect :5406, data-out push connect :5407 (136-138).
//   --task-name PixelFindHits is the default (14), so the program makes FairMQPixelTaskProcessor<PixelFindHits>
//   (run/runPixelTaskProcessor.cxx:21, 47).
//   ProcessData() is the OnData callback of data-in (FairMQPixelTaskProcessor.h:170). fCurrentRunId starts at -1 (37),
//   so at the first message, and when the run ID of the event header changes (--static-pars is false by default,
//   run/runPixelTaskProcessor.cxx:36), it calls UpdateParameters() (88-105):
//   one request "<name>,<run ID>" and one reply for each container of the list (184-217). The list holds
//   FairGeoParSet and the containers of the task (160-165), for PixelFindHits "PixelDigiParameters"
//   (src/PixelFindHits.cxx:145-149). Then ExecMQ() runs the task (110), and the header and the output go to data-out
//   (118-136).
// - Sink: pixel-sink --id pixDet-sink1, data-in pull bind tcp://*:5407 (147-149), a FairMQPixelFileSink
//   (run/runPixelFileSink.cxx:28). StoreData() fills the tree "cbmsim" (FairMQPixelFileSink.cxx:34-55, 57-81).
// - The ack channel: only with --command static (127-129, 150-152): sampler ack pull bind :5408, sink ack push
//   connect :5408. The sink sends one empty message for each stored message (FairMQPixelFileSink.cxx:83-86). The
//   sampler counts the acks in a thread up to the number of events, and PostRun() waits for that thread
//   (FairMQPixelSampler.cxx:91-98, 125-147). The static script waits until the sampler ends, then stops the other
//   devices and compares the events in the input and output file (script 236-295).
// - A push socket sends each message to the next connected pull socket in turn (ZeroMQ push/pull, round-robin).
//
// split: examples/MQ/pixelSimSplit/run/scripts/test-splitMQ.sh.in (the same channels as splitMC-topology.xml)
// - Channels (24-42) and devices (48-71): generator (pixel-sim-gen) primariesChannel push bind, ack pull bind;
//   transporter (pixel-sim-transport) primariesChannel pull connect, data#all# push connect, updateChannel req
//   connect; merger (pixel-sim-chunk-merger) data#all# pull bind, dataOut push bind; filesink (pixel-sink) dataOut
//   pull connect, ack push connect; parmq-server updateChannel rep bind. Addresses are ipc://. The script starts one
//   transporter, the DDS topology a group with n="1" (splitMC-topology.xml:54).
// - Generator: FairMQPrimaryGeneratorDevice (run/runMQGen.cxx:59) with a box generator of 100 pions per event
//   (runMQGen.cxx:49-57) and --chunk-size 10 (script 10): 100 / 10 = 10 chunks per event. One message for each chunk:
//   the header with the chunk range and all primaries (FairMQPrimaryGeneratorDevice.cxx:76-126). It counts the acks up
//   to --nof-events 100 (script 8) and PostRun() waits for them (128-149). The script waits for the generator (93-99).
// - Transporter: FairMQTransportDevice (run/runMQTrans.cxx:57-58, pull mode). The first PreRun() calls InitializeRun():
//   "ReportSimDevice" on updateChannel, reply "<run ID>_<device number>", then one request with each parameter
//   container, and SendObject() waits for each reply (FairMQTransportDevice.cxx:143-199, 253-271;
//   pixelDetector/src/devices/FairMQRunDevice.cxx:46-60). The server replies with the run ID, or stores the container
//   and replies SUCCESS (ParameterMQServer.cxx:166-227). TransportData() simulates the chunk with ProcessRun(1)
//   (FairMQTransportDevice.cxx:232-251). FairOnlineSink::Fill() calls SendBranches(), which sends the branches on each
//   channel with "#all#" in the name (pixelDetector/src/FairOnlineSink.cxx:47-55, FairMQRunDevice.cxx:62-120).
// - Merger: FairMQChunkMerger keeps the parts of an event until it has GetNofChunks() of them, merges them and sends one
//   message on its out channel (FairMQChunkMerger.cxx:44-50, 52-196).
// - Filesink: the FairMQPixelFileSink of the pixel example, with an ack for each event (see above).
//
// serialization: examples/MQ/serialization/startSerializationEx.sh.in
// - sampler1 (ex-serialization-sampler) data1 push bind tcp://localhost:5565; processor1 and processor2
//   (ex-serialization-processor) data1 pull connect :5565, data2 push connect :5570; sink1 (ex-serialization-sink)
//   data2 pull bind tcp://localhost:5570 (8-30). Programs: CMakeLists.txt:43-50.
// - sampler.cxx:63-79: part 0 an ExHeader with BoostSerializer<ExHeader>, part 1 the TClonesArray of MyDigi of the
//   tree cbmsim with RootSerializer (a TMessage, RootSerializer.h:41-48). processor.cxx:35-63: FindHits() makes MyHit
//   objects; part 0 is the received header part, part 1 the hits with BoostSerializer<MyHit>, a Boost archive of a
//   std::vector<MyHit> (BoostSerializer.h:90-111). sink.cxx:30-60: fills the tree "SerializationEx". The two
//   serializers are in fairroot/basemq/policies/Serialization/.
//
// Motion: one shared event simulation; durations come from the route lengths of the visible layout. The timing is
// illustrative. Reduced motion: a static picture, and the Play button starts the motion.
interface Props {
  example?: 'pixel' | 'split' | 'serialization';
}
const ex = (['pixel', 'split', 'serialization'] as const).find((e) => e === Astro.props.example) ?? 'pixel';

type P = [number, number];
type C = 'd' | 'p' | 'a'; // data, request/reply, ack
type Seg = string | { c: string }; // text, or a code name
type Txt = { id: string; cls: string; does: Seg[]; srv?: boolean; meter?: boolean };
type Box = { k: string; x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number };
type Route = { c: C; pts: P[]; dash?: boolean };
type Port = [number, number, C, boolean]; // x, y, kind, binds
type Lbl = { x: number; y: number; a: 'start' | 'middle' | 'end'; t: [string, string][] }; // [class, text]
type Layout = { id: 'wide' | 'narrow'; W: number; H: number; boxes: Box[]; routes: Record<string, Route>; ports: Port[]; lbls: Lbl[] };
type Still = { toks: [string, number, string][]; busy: string[]; meter?: number };
type Example = {
  src: string;
  info: Seg[];
  aria: string;
  txt: Record<string, Txt>;
  wide: Layout;
  narrow: Layout;
  still: Still;
  key: string[];
};

const L = (x: number, y: number, a: Lbl['a'], ...t: [string, string][]): Lbl => ({ x, y, a, t });
const B = (k: string, x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number): Box => ({ k, x, y, w, h });
const proc = (n: number, cls: string, does: Seg[]): Txt => ({ id: `pixDet-processor${n}`, cls, does });

